  "findings": "The adopted 2026–2027 regulations, current Study Guide and linked timetable establish a 180 EC full-time route. The Algebra and Geometry study path is one set of recommended choices. Year one has 60 EC of required courses. Year two has 30 EC of required courses, 6 EC in Elements of Geometry as the period-six choice and 24 EC of mathematics choices. Year three has 30 EC of open study, 12 EC of mathematics choices, two 3 EC courses and a 12 EC Bachelor Project. The project requires 120 EC after December results and comprises a supervised mathematical investigation, English thesis and oral presentation. The assessment weights are 50% thesis, 30% performance and 20% presentation; the thesis must earn at least 5.5. Passing Study and Career is required for Elements of Geometry credits. The English diagnostic adds no credits. The older recruitment-page reference to Project Mathematics is superseded by the current regulations.",
  "authority": "Adopted 10 July 2026, Mathematics TER arts. 9.1, 11.3, 12.1 and 15.2, current annual guide, exact X_400581 project module and official Algebra and Geometry study path timetable. The two 38-row registry sets repeat the interests and are both assessed without doubling academic weight. The adopted rules replace the discontinued Project Mathematics still mentioned on the recruitment page."
